1. COMMANDER DECISION

As Human Commander, I hereby approve and direct the implementation of:

DEVELOPMENT AUTHORITY RECONCILIATION 001

This decision establishes the approved direction for restoring Rallyproof’s normal delegated professional development operating model.

The governing principle is:

COMMANDER LEADS.

SECTIONS EXECUTE.

DEVELOPMENT TOOLS ARE INTERCHANGEABLE.

Commander establishes the mission, objectives, boundaries and reserved decisions.

Competent sections lead and execute ordinary development within their effective delegated authority.

Ordinary development shall not require repeated personal Commander approvals for individual technical execution steps or qualified routine pull requests.

I hereby approve the prospective establishment of:

1. Standing bounded ordinary integration authority delegated to the existing S6 function.
2. Standing bounded Build Hold coverage for authorized ordinary non-production repository development.
3. Prospective transition provisions for eligible existing campaigns and tasks.
4. Consolidated development-tool independence consistent with previously effective simplifications.
5. Technical currentness reconciliation without unnecessary substantive Commander reauthorization.

ALL FIVE DIRECTIONS ARE APPROVED.

This decision constitutes substantive Commander approval of the defined reconciliation.

No further substantive Commander approval of this operating model is required solely to implement these approved provisions.

Competent normative integration, independent qualification and prospective effectivity remain required before the new delegations become exercisable.

