5. STANDING BOUNDED GRANT C — S6 INTEGRATION DELEGATION

5.1 Commander approval

APPROVED.

Human Commander expressly approves the prospective establishment of standing bounded ordinary repository integration authority delegated to the existing:

S6 — ENGINEERING & TECHNICAL SYSTEMS

S6 is the competent existing technical function selected to receive this delegation.

No new integration role, service or organizational authority holder shall be created.

5.2 Delegation scope

After competent normative integration and prospective effectivity, S6 may determine ordinary integration readiness and authorize qualified normal repository merges within an effective development campaign or task.

The delegation applies only to ordinary non-production repository development within authorized scope.

It does not create universal merge authority.

5.3 S6 delegated integration responsibilities

Within the effective delegation, S6 may:

1. Verify effective task and campaign authority.
2. Verify that the PR remains within authorized scope.
3. Verify technical currentness and compatibility.
4. Verify applicable CI and tests.
5. Verify required independent review.
6. Verify applicable Build Hold coverage.
7. Verify GEAI and material-change boundaries.
8. Issue an attributable ordinary integration disposition.
9. Authorize the corresponding exact GitHub mutation where permitted by applicable protected execution requirements.
10. Coordinate required independent postmerge verification.

Each PR shall have an attributable integration determination based on existing applicable evidence.

This determination is a delegated operational decision.

It is not a new substantive Commander decision.

No additional universal review gate is created.

5.4 Technical mutation

The actual GitHub merge shall be performed by an authenticated and authorized technical executor.

The merge shall satisfy applicable exact mutation authorization, currentness, CI, independent review, branch protection and provenance requirements.

Where the effective standing delegation expressly permits S6 to issue the required exact mutation authorization, S6 may do so within that delegation.

An executor shall not infer authority from repository access alone.

An executor shall not self-authorize or self-qualify where applicable controls prohibit it.

5.5 Grant C exclusions

The delegation does not authorize:

* Governance authority amendments.
* Protected methodology changes.
* Security-policy changes.
* Database or Writer mutations.
* Production deployment.
* Customer publication or release.
* Branch-protection bypass.
* Unauthorized protected-state mutations.
* Other Commander-reserved operations.

These remain governed by their competent authority.

5.6 Stop conditions

Missing authority, failed mandatory review, failed required CI, material conflict, stale protected binding, expired authority, revocation or unauthorized scope means:

NO MERGE.

Required postmerge verification remains applicable.

MERGED DOES NOT MEAN EFFECTIVE.

MERGED DOES NOT MEAN DEPLOYED.

